--TEST--
A value that cannot cross a copy boundary is refused by `Core\Topic::publish` whether or not anybody joined the topic — `rule:core-classes/topic`, ADR 0033 § 1, `rule:classes/graph-copy`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// § 4 copies a published value by `rule:classes/graph-copy`'s graph copy, and that walk does
// two jobs: it gives every subscriber a value shared with nobody, and it
// refuses what has no meaning on the other side. Only the first of those
// scales with the audience, so the refusal is made once and *before* the walk.
// A rule that held or did not by who happened to be listening would be no
// rule -- and this script is why it has to be that way round: nothing here is
// a connection, so no case in this corpus can ever have a subscriber, and a
// refusal behind the fan-out would be unreachable from every one of them.
class Credential {
    public string $who = "ana";
    public secret string $token = "s3cr3t";
}

Credential $held = new Credential();
try {
    Core\Topic::publish("room:lobby", $held);
    echo "published\n";
} catch (LogicError $refused) {
    echo $refused->message, "\n";
}

// ADR 0033: it is the qualifier that is refused and not the object. The same
// two fields without it cross, and answer the count nobody is.
class Profile {
    public string $who = "ana";
    public string $token = "s3cr3t";
}

Profile $open = new Profile();
echo Core\Topic::publish("room:lobby", $open), "\n";
--EXPECT--
`Core\Topic::publish` cannot publish this value: Credential::$token is `secret` and does not cross a copy boundary unless it is revealed
0
